{#
| Variable     | Type                  | Description |
|--------------|-----------------------|-------------|
| page         | Page                  |             |
| page.title   | string                |             |
| page.content | string                |             |
| page.url     | string                |             |
| page.slug    | string                |             |
| page.type    | string                |             |
#}
{#
  T-7.01 — the shell every CMS page shares. Technique A.

  ONE TEMPLATE, THREE JOBS, AND THE THIRD IS THE ONE THAT NEEDED A RULING.

    · an ordinary CMS page — Shipping, Return & Exchange, How to Order, and
      whatever the merchant writes next. A prose card, and the prose styles are
      declared **once**, in `04-components/prose.scss`, rather than per page.
    · a `customised` page — Salla's own component-composed page type, whose
      blocks arrive through the `information_page` hook. Untouched, because that
      hook is the platform's mechanism for it.
    · **the stories feed.** Ruled by the owner on 2026-08-08 (OP-3, reading 2):
      Salla's page set is fixed and a theme cannot mint a `/stories` route, so
      «تجارب عملائنا» gets its URL from a CMS page the merchant creates, named by
      the `stories_page_id` setting. **No slug is hard-coded anywhere** — the
      merchant names the page and the setting names its id.

  THE FEED ITSELF IS NOT REBUILT HERE, AND COULD NOT BE. The story items live in
  the `home.stories` component's own collection, which is bound only while that
  component renders — so the page shows the feed by the merchant **placing that
  component on the page**, which is what a `customised` page is for. This template
  adds the two things the feed page has and the Home section does not, both drawn
  on `Customer Stories – Pinterest Style.pdf` and on neither Home artboard: the
  **category chips** and the **brand dropdown**. `components.stories.story-card`
  and `.stories__grid` are consumed exactly as they are.

  THE CONTROLS ARE A MOUNT POINT HERE AND MARKUP IN `stories-filter.js`, WHICH IS
  A SPLIT WITH A REASON. Their options are the distinct brands and tags of
  whatever stories the merchant placed — knowable only from the rendered cards,
  since this template cannot reach the component's collection. Twig therefore owns
  **where** they go and the script owns **what** is in them. Without the script
  there are no controls and every story is visible, which is the correct
  degradation for a filter; a rendered-but-empty chip row would be a control that
  lies.

  THE CARD IS `.account-panel`, SAMPLED RATHER THAN CHOSEN. `Return & Exchange.pdf`
  at 200dpi: the card fills `#F7F6F4` inside a 1px `#646361` edge — exactly
  `--surface-section` on `--border-interactive`, which is the surface T-5.08
  declared and T-5.10, T-6.01 and T-6.07 have each reused since. No new box.
#}
{% extends "layouts.master" %}

{% set stories_page_id = theme.settings.get('stories_page_id') %}
{% set is_stories_page = stories_page_id and page.id == stories_page_id %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="container">
        <nav class="static-page__breadcrumb" aria-label="{{ trans('theme.customer.breadcrumb') }}">
            <salla-breadcrumb></salla-breadcrumb>
        </nav>
    </div>

    {% if page.type == 'customised' %}
        {#
          The stories controls, above the blocks the merchant placed. `.container`
          of their own because the hook's own sections each bring one.
        #}
        {% if is_stories_page %}
            <div class="container">
                <div data-stories-controls></div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

        {#
          Hook: information_page.information_page
          Fires before the main informative page content section.
          Use this hook to inject custom content or components above the page content area.
        #}
        <div class="s-blocks-wrapper s-information-page !mt-0">{% hook 'information_page.information_page' %}</div>
    {% else %}
        <div class="container">
            <article class="account-panel static-page">
                <h1 class="static-page__title">{{ page.title }}</h1>

                {#
                  The merchant's rich text. `|raw` is upstream's and is correct —
                  it is the store's own moderated content — and the prose styles
                  that shape it live in one stylesheet rather than being restated
                  by each page that happens to use them.
                #}
                <div class="content-entry">
                    {{ page.content|raw }}
                </div>
            </article>

            <salla-comments data-testid="store-page-comments" item-id="{{ page.id }}" type="page"></salla-comments>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
    {% if is_stories_page %}
        {#
          `home.js` already says this: «T-7.01 must import it from whichever
          bundle serves the stories page rather than copying it». The `stories`
          entry is that bundle — the hotspot primitive, the story modal and this
          page's filter, and **not** the whole Home bundle, which would drag
          lite-youtube, fslightbox and the video carousel onto a page of
          photographs.
        #}
        <script defer src="{{ 'stories.js' | asset }}"></script>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
